## Overview
Investigated novel biomarkers for early diagnosis of acute kidney injury (AKI) caused by pesticides, chemicals, and envenomation. This work focused on identifying sensitive molecular markers that can detect kidney damage before conventional clinical indicators become abnormal.Key Achievements
Developed quantitative bedside methemoglobin colour chart
Reduced propanil poisoning mortality from 9.5% to 3.1%
Incorporated into national clinical guidelines
Adopted internationally as a low-cost diagnostic tool

##Key Achievements
•	Led Renal Biomarker Program at SACTRC
•	Identified urinary and circulating biomarkers for nephrotoxicity
•	Established laboratory workflows for multicentre clinical studies
•	Supported international collaborations in toxicology and nephrology

## Publications

* Ann Emerg Med. 2010
* Bull World Health Organ. 2016
